# Sources, Licenses, and Notices

Ethoculus is an early-stage, local-first generative AI starter platform focused on practical installation, document-aware workflows, source checking, and responsible public use.

This page explains the project’s attribution, licensing, and third-party component notices.

---

## Project Origin

This repository began from the open-source LAION Open Assistant project.

Open Assistant was an important open-source effort to make chat-based large language model technology more accessible. The upstream Open Assistant project has been completed.

Ethoculus is a new project direction. It should not be represented as the original LAION Open Assistant project.

Original upstream project:

- [LAION Open Assistant](https://github.com/LAION-AI/Open-Assistant)

---

## Ethoculus Project Direction

Ethoculus focuses on:

- Local-first installation
- Simple model setup
- Docker-based deployment
- Ollama model support
- Open WebUI integration
- Document-aware RAG workflows
- Source verification
- Ethical AI use
- Human review and accountability

The Ethoculus rule:

> Check the sources. Validate the outputs. Question the machine. Protect the people most likely to be harmed by automation.

